      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "NO. 1 ATLANTIC DRIVE, LISDOONVARNA, CO. CLARE V95 D2V5\r\n\r\nSEMI DETACHED BUNGALOW - PART OF A PRIVATE ‘CUL DE SAC’ MATURE DEVELOPMENT!\r\nViewings strictly by appointment with sole agent Streets Ahead Properties\r\n\r\nCompany Licence No. 003178\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\n\r\nAt Streets Ahead Properties, we are truly delighted to be able to present No. 1 Atlantic Drive, Lisdoonvarna, Co. Clare, a charming, semi-detached 3-bedroom bungalow. The property extends to 84.91 sq.m. /913.96 sq.ft and boasts a low maintenance garden at the rear and side of the house.\r\n\r\nNo. 1 Atlantic Drive is located within a mature residential, ‘cul de sac’ development on the outskirts of Lisdoonvarna town. This impressive semi-detached home has the extra benefit of occupying an end site in a very quiet and peaceful location. Ease of access to all local amenities including primary and secondary schools.  As this property is located on Irelands famed ‘Wild Atlantic Way’, it boasts a variety of beaches along our rugged coastline on the doorstep with excellent connection routes to all towns and villages nearby. \r\n\r\nThis residence is located 1.6km from Lisdoonvarna town or a 3 minute drive allowing ease of access to all amenities within the town. This property can be accessed from the R476 main Lisdoonvarna/Kilfenora route. \r\n\r\nAccommodation is comprised of an entrance porch, sitting room, kitchen/dining room, 3 bedrooms, corridor, main bathroom and hot press. Low maintenance garden at the rear of the property. Gated entrance. Double glazed PVC windows and doors. Solid fuel stove in sitting room with a back boiler heating water and radiators. Additional sold fuel stove in the kitchen/dining room.\r\n\r\nApproximate floor area   84.91 sq. meters (913.96 sq. ft.) \r\nBER G. \r\nYear of construction: 1977.\r\n\r\nLisdoonvarna is a spa town in North Clare on the road from Ennistymon to Ballvaughan. It is well known for its month-long September festival and the Burren Slow Food Festival. Lisdoonvarna is perfectly placed for visits to the Burren National Park. Primary and Secondary Schools on the doorstep. The town offers shops, a pharmacy, medical facilities, hotels, bars, restaurants, post office and the widely known Burren Smokehouse famous for its smoked Salmon worldwide.\r\n\r\nThis is an ideal opportunity for a first-time buyer. Early viewing is highly recommended Viewings strictly by advance appointment with sole agent Streets Ahead Properties. \r\n\r\nLOCAL AREAS OF ATTRACTION: \r\n\r\nDoolin, Co Clare is famous for its traditional music sessions almost every night of the year. This area is hugely popular with tourists, in fact it is one of the premier tourist destinations along the Wild Atlantic Way just 6km north of the Cliffs of Moher and a gateway to the award-winning UNESCO geopark, which includes the Burren & the Cliffs of Moher. Doolin is within a 10-minute drive of the property. \r\n\r\nFanore village is accessible in less than 20 minutes from this property - offering the most fantastic breathtaking views of Galway Bay and the Aran Islands, Fanore is considered to be one of the most scenic areas of Co. Clare. Fanore village offers wonderful opportunities for exploring.  Walking, cycling, rock climbing and a host of water sports such as surfing, kayaking and angling are just some of the activities available for enjoyment. \r\n\r\nLahinch, famous for its 2km sandy beach and 18-hole Championship Golf Course is approximately a 15.8 km approximately a 20 minute drive. Lahinch is popular throughout the year and has become a surfer’s haven in recent years. An ideal spot for family outings. \r\n\r\nLiscannor is a small fishing village where seafood is a speciality in the local hotels and restaurants, less than a 20 minute drive from the property.\r\n\r\nEnnistymon, is the main market town of North Clare renowned for its traditional shop fronts. Ennistymon is a thriving business town with an abundance of character. Accessible in 15 mins from the property.\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION - APPROXIMATE DIMENSIONS:\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway: (2.97m x 1.37m) Tiled flooring. Spacious. Allows access to the kitchen and also to the sitting room.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining: (2.52m x 2.39m) Tiled flooring accessed from front hallway entrance and also by a side door, solid wood burning stove on raised level, brick surround and Liscannor flag base, fitted kitchen wall and base units, tiled splashback, fridge, washing machine and electric cooker with extractor.\r\n\r\nSitting room: (4.77m x 4.15m) (3.16m x 2.18m) Front aspect, carpeted flooring, also accessible from entrance hallway, open fireplace, timber mantle and surround, cast iron insert on a granite base. Bright cosy room with ample natural light.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: (4.52m x 2.89m) Rear aspect and complete with carpeted flooring, fitted wardrobes, W.H.B. and storage underneath. This room is very generous in size.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: (3.01 x 2.75m) Double bedroom complete with carpeted flooring and fitted wardrobe, rear aspect.\r\nRecessed wardrobe: (0.82 m x 0.6m) \r\n\r\nBedroom 3: (3.27m x 2.73m) Twin room, rear aspect, carpeted flooring, fitted wardrobe.\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom: (2.23m x 1.67m) Tiled flooring, high gloss vinyl wall cladding, bath and electric shower overhead with glass panel shower door, W.C. and W.H.B.\r\n\r\nCorridor: (4.04m x 0.92m) Carpeted flooring.\r\n\r\nHotpress: (1.41m x 0.67m) (0.73m x 0.66m)\r\n\r\nExternal\r\n\r\nFirst house on the left as you enter this mature ‘cul de sac’ development. Gated entrance with concrete parking space. Low maintenance garden to the side and rear of the property, neat lawns to the front. Mains water and sewer."
      },
